  "correction_rules": [
    "Model tends to overestimate prices in the short term (1-3 days) after recent spikes, especially when sentiment is neutral or slightly positive.",
    "Significant overshoots in forecasted prices are followed by strong mean reversion, suggesting a correction rule: reduce forecast by 5-15% of the peak value within 5-7 days.",
    "When sentiment remains flat (0.00) over 18+ days, model exhibits persistent bias — adjust forecast downward by 2-5% of the 30-day average to account for lack of momentum.",
    "Model underestimates prices during downward trends, particularly when true outcomes show sharp declines — apply a lag correction: add 1-3% to forecast for 3-5 days to account for delayed reaction.",
    "Forecast horizon > 14 days shows increasing underestimation of price drops — apply a downward bias correction of 3-7% for long-term forecasts when sentiment is neutral or negative."
  ]
